hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1318","Musa bin Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi told us, Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Burayd, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: “If one of you passes through our mosque or our market carrying a arrow, let him hold its arrows with his palm so as not to hit any of the Muslims.” “Some of it,” or he said, “Let him seize its roots.”"
